                <pb facs="0528" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg408"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Dawson.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Strongly advisé President to avoid rupture with cabinet. We are not willing to
                    give instructions to admiral based on assumption that Vice-President and cabinet
                    will create situation requiring our intervention for the protection of American
                    citizens.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Root.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
